# Netlify Redirect Rules for React Router SPA
# This rule rewrites ALL paths (/*) to /index.html with status 200.
# Why: Netlify serves static files. Without this, direct navigation or refresh on
# routes like /login, /system-admin/login, /program-admin/login, /evaluator/login,
# /accepted-dashboard, etc. would 404 because those files do not physically exist.
# The 200 status makes it a rewrite (not a redirect), so the browser URL stays as-is
# and React Router can parse and render the correct route client-side.
# Place this file in the deploy root (public/ for CRA). Netlify copies it to the build output.
# If you add server-side functions later, put more specific rules ABOVE this catch-all.

/*    /index.html   200
